course: dictionary
lesson: 9931
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings. Tap is a good example. The words around it, its context, tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «She had to tap the screen to choose a game.» Here tap means to touch something lightly and quickly. In «a tap on the door», a tap is a light knock. It is the same word with a different meaning.
explain: A tap can also be a thing: the tap in the kitchen is where water comes out. People in the UK say tap, but Americans say faucet. When you meet tap, ask what fits the sentence, then try your meaning in it.
fact: Tap has several meanings, so check the context.
fact: A tap (UK) is a thing you turn to let water come out. Americans say faucet.
fact: To tap means to touch something lightly and quickly, as in «tap the screen».
fact: A tap is also a light knock, as in «a tap on the door».
fact: «On tap» means ready to use. Tap dancing is dancing with metal plates on your shoes.
exercise: «She had to tap the screen to choose a game.» What does tap mean here? | Hit it hard to break it | Dance on it with metal plates | *Touch it lightly and quickly | Turn it on to let water out
exercise: A tap fills a bucket at 2 litres per minute. How many minutes to fill 10 litres? | 20 minutes | 3 minutes | *5 minutes | 8 minutes
exercise: Which word do Americans use for a tap? | Sink | Drain | *Faucet | Bin
test: Why should you turn off the tap while you brush your teeth? | *To save water | To make the tap dance | To make the water warmer | To stop the water tasting of toothpaste
test: In «a tap on the door», what is a tap? | A tap in the kitchen | A drop of rain | *A light knock | A metal plate on a shoe
exam: What is «tap water»? | Sparkling water from a bottle | Rain that falls on roofs | *Water that comes from a tap | Salty sea water
